course: dictionary
lesson: 8852
title: Shoebox: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them show you which meaning fits. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one makes sense. «Mila keeps every letter in a shoebox with a ribbon round it.» Here a shoebox is a box for storing things, because she keeps letters in it.
explain: A shoebox can be the cardboard box that new shoes come in. It can also be a box for storing small things or for making crafts and school projects. «Small pets are often buried in the garden, in a shoebox or wrapped in a cloth, with a stone or a cross on top, as a small funeral.» Here the clues show it is a box holding something small, not a box for shoes.
explain: The third meaning is informal. A shoebox can mean a very small room or flat. If a sentence describes a tiny home with no space to move, this meaning may fit. Always check the clues before you choose.
fact: A shoebox is the cardboard box that new shoes come in.
fact: A shoebox can be used to store small things, such as photos, toys or cards.
fact: At school, a shoebox diorama is a small scene built inside a box for a science or reading project.
fact: Informally, «shoebox» can mean a very small room or flat.
fact: A shoebox gift appeal is a way of collecting gifts, put into shoeboxes.
exercise: «Mila keeps every letter in a shoebox with a ribbon round it.» What is the shoebox used for here? | To wear on your feet | To grow plants in | To run races in | *To store letters and keep them safe
exercise: For a science project, Sam builds a small scene inside a box, with tiny trees and a pond. What do we call a small scene built inside a box? | A jigsaw | A road map | A shoelace | *A shoebox diorama
exercise: Ella says, «The new flat is so tiny, it's just a shoebox.» What does shoebox mean here? | *A very small room or flat | A box of new shoes | A school bag | A big park with lots of trees
test: In «She found an old photo in a shoebox under the bed», what is a shoebox? | A wooden bed frame | A shoe shop on the high street | A cupboard for coats | *A box that stores small things, like photos
test: What can «shoebox» mean informally? | A box of cereal | A pair of new trainers | *A very small room or flat | A giant cardboard castle
exam: The sentence says, «Priya's reading project was a shoebox diorama of the story.» What is a shoebox here? | A box for posting letters | *A small box used for a school project | A box of shoes from the shop | A tiny flat in the city
